    "title": "problem: don't send an invitation to a team if the user is already member of the org",
    "body": "### Does your problem still exist on the latest Forgejo version?\n\nYes, the problem still exists (tested on a next instance)\n\n### About your usage of Forgejo\n\nwetneb/todo#5\n\n### Problem description\n\nOn an instance with `ADD_MEMBERS_BY_INVITATIONS = true`, invitations are sent out when a user is added to a team.\r\nBut if the team is part of an organization that the user is already a member of, this is perhaps a bit heavy. They have already consented to being part of the org (and potentially that org membership being made public).\r\n\r\nIn such a case, I would expect the member to be added to the team directly.\n\n### Potential workarounds\n\nnone\n\n### Forgejo Version\n\n15.0.9-6-85b0721bc6\n\n### Other details about your environment (software names and versions)\n\nirrelevant\n\n### Solutions\n\n*Accepted solutions to address this problem will go here*\n\n\n",
